<owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/nexusformat/definitions/Field/NXcorrector_cs/TABLEAU/model">
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="#NeXusField"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf>
    <owl:Restriction>
      <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="#actualValue"/>
      <owl:allValuesFrom>
        <rdfs:Datatype>
          <owl:oneOf>
            <rdf:Description>
          <rdf:first rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ceos</rdf:first>
            <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
            </rdf:Description>
          </owl:oneOf>
        </rdfs:Datatype>
      </owl:allValuesFrom>
    </owl:Restriction>
  </rdfs:subClassOf>
  <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">NXcorrector_cs/TABLEAU/model</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">
                Convention used for storing measured or estimated aberrations (for each image or final)
                via fields c_1, a_1, c_1_0, c_1_2_a, and so on and so forth.
                
                See `S. J. Pennycock and P. D. Nellist &lt;https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4419-7200-2&gt;`_ (page 44ff, and page 118ff)
                for different definitions available and further details. Table 7-2 of Ibid. publication (page 305ff) documents how
                to convert from the Nion to the CEOS definitions. Conversion tables are also summarized by `Y. Liao &lt;https://www.globalsino.com/EM/page3740.html&gt;`_.
            </rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">https://manual.nexusformat.org/classes/contributed_definitions/NXcorrector_cs.html#nxcorrector-cs-tableau-model-field</rdfs:seeAlso>
</owl:Class>

